      "writtenOn": "2019-11-21T20:53:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "What are you looking for in terms of error propagation? It looks like the callers of this are just testing for !0 and then returning an error.\n\nIn inet_autobind(), this would result in -EAGAIN back to userspace... would you prefer a less transient sounding error for this case? Maybe -EINVAL?\n\nIn __inet_bind(), this would result in -EADDRINUSE. Maybe -EINVAL for this one too?\n\nIn inet_csk_listen_start(), I\u0027m not sure what would be returned (whatever comes back from sk_prot-\u003ehash(sk)).",
